1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,167
Night five. 3:09 AM. The bell rings
once. Rule three said that's normal.

2
00:00:05,867 --> 00:00:09,067
A man walks in. Old jacket. Wet boots.
No car in the lot.

3
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:12,500
He's not a customer. He's walking
straight at me.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,433
Rule eleven. At 3:10 he comes. Sell
him one coffee. Black. No receipt.

5
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:18,567
Coffee.

6
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:22,533
One coffee. Black. No receipt.

7
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:27,933
His hand trembles. The cup is warm. He
drinks it slowly, standing at the
counter.

8
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:31,100
Rule twelve. Never ask him why he
comes.

9
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:34,000
Every question I have starts with why.

10
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,400
He holds the cup with both hands, like
it's the only warm thing he's touched
in years.

11
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,800
His boots are wet, but there's no
puddle under them.

12
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:44,033
Thank you.

13
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:49,300
He leaves. The bell rings once. No
footsteps in the rain.
